# Real-World Incident
A fintech API encrypted sensitive fields with a hard-coded AES key and reused IVs; an attacker who obtained a container image layer recovered the key and decrypted stored tokens.

## Vulnerable Implementation

```java
// VULNERABLE: Hardcoded encryption keys and weak algorithms
package com.example.security;

import javax.crypto.Cipher;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;
import java.util.Base64;

public class CryptoService {

    // VULNERABLE: Hardcoded encryption key in source code
    private static final String SECRET_KEY = "MySecretKey12345"; // 16 bytes

    // VULNERABLE: Using weak DES algorithm (deprecated since 2005)
    private static final String ALGORITHM = "DES";

    public String encrypt(String data) throws Exception {
        // VULNERABLE: DES uses 56-bit keys (easily brute forced)
        // VULNERABLE: No IV/salt - same plaintext = same ciphertext
        SecretKeySpec keySpec = new SecretKeySpec(SECRET_KEY.getBytes(), ALGORITHM);
        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(ALGORITHM);
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, keySpec);

        byte[] encrypted = cipher.doFinal(data.getBytes());
        return Base64.getEncoder().encodeToString(encrypted);
    }

    public String decrypt(String encryptedData) throws Exception {
        SecretKeySpec keySpec = new SecretKeySpec(SECRET_KEY.getBytes(), ALGORITHM);
        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(ALGORITHM);
        cipher.init(Cipher.DECRYPT_MODE, keySpec);

        byte[] decrypted = cipher.doFinal(Base64.getDecoder().decode(encryptedData));
        return new String(decrypted);
    }
}
```

### Attack Demonstration

**Step 1: Extract hardcoded key**
```bash
# Attacker decompiles JAR file
jar -xf application.jar
javap -c com/example/security/CryptoService.class

# Finds hardcoded key: "MySecretKey12345"
```

**Step 2: Decrypt all encrypted data**
```java
// Attacker uses extracted key to decrypt everything
CryptoService attacker = new CryptoService();
String decrypted = attacker.decrypt(stolenCiphertext);
// All "encrypted" data is now plaintext
```

**Impact:**
- All encrypted data is compromised
- DES crackable in hours with modern hardware
- Hardcoded keys cannot be rotated
- Same key across all environments (dev, staging, prod)

## Common Mistakes

1. **Using fast hash functions for passwords** — Using MD5, SHA-1, or SHA-256 for password storage. These are fast hash functions designed for integrity checking, not password storage. Attackers crack them at billions of attempts per second.

2. **Hardcoded encryption keys** — Storing encryption keys in source code, environment variables at build time, or configuration files committed to Git. Use dedicated secrets managers (AWS Secrets Manager, HashiCorp Vault).

3. **Rolling your own crypto** — Implementing custom encryption, token generation, or key derivation instead of using established libraries (bcrypt, argon2, libsodium). Custom crypto invariably contains flaws.

4. **Ignoring key rotation** — Never rotating encryption keys, API keys, or JWT signing secrets. If a key leaks, every historical encrypted value is compromised.

## Secure Implementation

### Tier 1: Critical Fix (5 min)

**Use AES-256-GCM with externalized keys and random IVs**

```java
// SECURE: Modern authenticated encryption with externalized keys
package com.example.security;

import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Value;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import javax.crypto.Cipher;
import javax.crypto.SecretKey;
import javax.crypto.spec.GCMParameterSpec;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;
import java.security.SecureRandom;
import java.util.Base64;

@Service
public class TokenEncryptionService {

    private static final String ALGORITHM = "AES";
    private static final String TRANSFORMATION = "AES/GCM/NoPadding";
    private static final int GCM_TAG_LENGTH = 128;
    private static final int GCM_IV_LENGTH = 12;

    // ✅ SECURE: Key loaded from environment (never hardcoded)
    @Value("${encryption.key.base64}")
    private String encodedKey;

    public String encryptToken(String token) throws Exception {
        SecretKey key = new SecretKeySpec(
            Base64.getDecoder().decode(encodedKey),
            ALGORITHM
        );

        // ✅ SECURE: Generate random IV for each encryption
        byte[] iv = new byte[GCM_IV_LENGTH];
        new SecureRandom().nextBytes(iv);

        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(TRANSFORMATION);
        GCMParameterSpec spec = new GCMParameterSpec(GCM_TAG_LENGTH, iv);
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key, spec);

        byte[] encrypted = cipher.doFinal(token.getBytes());

        // Prepend IV to ciphertext for decryption
        byte[] combined = new byte[iv.length + encrypted.length];
        System.arraycopy(iv, 0, combined, 0, iv.length);
        System.arraycopy(encrypted, 0, combined, iv.length, encrypted.length);

        return Base64.getEncoder().encodeToString(combined);
    }

    public String decryptToken(String encryptedToken) throws Exception {
        byte[] combined = Base64.getDecoder().decode(encryptedToken);

        // Extract IV and ciphertext
        byte[] iv = new byte[GCM_IV_LENGTH];
        byte[] encrypted = new byte[combined.length - GCM_IV_LENGTH];
        System.arraycopy(combined, 0, iv, 0, iv.length);
        System.arraycopy(combined, iv.length, encrypted, 0, encrypted.length);

        SecretKey key = new SecretKeySpec(
            Base64.getDecoder().decode(encodedKey),
            ALGORITHM
        );

        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(TRANSFORMATION);
        GCMParameterSpec spec = new GCMParameterSpec(GCM_TAG_LENGTH, iv);
        cipher.init(Cipher.DECRYPT_MODE, key, spec);

        byte[] decrypted = cipher.doFinal(encrypted);
        return new String(decrypted);
    }
}
```

**Configuration (application.properties)**
```properties
# ✅ Key loaded from environment variable
encryption.key.base64=${ENCRYPTION_KEY}

# Generate 256-bit AES key:
# keytool -genseckey -alias tokenkey -keyalg AES -keysize 256 \
#   -storetype PKCS12 -keystore keystore.p12
# Then export and base64 encode for environment variable
```

### Tier 2: Essential Defenses (15 min)

**Add key rotation, versioning, and audit logging**

```java
// SECURE: Key rotation with versioned encryption
package com.example.security;

import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import org.slf4j.Logger;
import org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;
import java.util.Map;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;

@Service
public class VersionedTokenEncryptionService {

    private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(VersionedTokenEncryptionService.class);
    private final Map<String, SecretKey> activeKeys = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    private String currentKeyId;

    public String encryptToken(String token) throws Exception {
        // ✅ Tag ciphertext with key version for rotation
        String keyId = currentKeyId;
        SecretKey key = activeKeys.get(keyId);

        if (key == null) {
            log.error("Encryption key not found: {}", keyId);
            throw new SecurityException("Encryption key unavailable");
        }

        String ciphertext = performEncryption(token, key);

        // Prepend key version for decryption
        return keyId + ":" + ciphertext;
    }

    public String decryptToken(String encryptedToken) throws Exception {
        // ✅ Extract key version and decrypt with appropriate key
        String[] parts = encryptedToken.split(":", 2);
        if (parts.length != 2) {
            log.warn("Invalid token format: missing key version");
            throw new SecurityException("Invalid encrypted token format");
        }

        String keyId = parts[0];
        String ciphertext = parts[1];

        SecretKey key = activeKeys.get(keyId);
        if (key == null) {
            log.error("Decryption key not found: {}", keyId);
            throw new SecurityException("Decryption key unavailable");
        }

        return performDecryption(ciphertext, key);
    }

    // ✅ Rotate keys without downtime
    public void rotateKey(String newKeyId, SecretKey newKey) {
        log.info("Rotating encryption key to version: {}", newKeyId);
        activeKeys.put(newKeyId, newKey);
        currentKeyId = newKeyId;

        // Keep old keys active for 30 days (decrypt legacy tokens)
        scheduleKeyRemoval(newKeyId, 30);
    }

    private void scheduleKeyRemoval(String keyId, int daysToKeep) {
        // Schedule key removal after grace period
        // Implementation depends on scheduler (Quartz, Spring @Scheduled, etc.)
    }
}

// Audit logging filter
package com.example.security;

import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;
import org.slf4j.Logger;
import org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;
import javax.servlet.*;
import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;
import java.io.IOException;

@Component
public class CryptoAuditFilter implements Filter {

    private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(CryptoAuditFilter.class);

    @Override
    public void doFilter(ServletRequest request, ServletResponse response, FilterChain chain)
            throws IOException, ServletException {

        HttpServletRequest httpRequest = (HttpServletRequest) request;
        String operation = httpRequest.getParameter("cryptoOp");

        // ✅ Log all encryption/decryption operations
        if ("encrypt".equals(operation) || "decrypt".equals(operation)) {
            log.info("Crypto operation: {} from IP: {} user: {}",
                operation,
                httpRequest.getRemoteAddr(),
                httpRequest.getUserPrincipal() != null ? 
                    httpRequest.getUserPrincipal().getName() : "anonymous");
        }

        chain.doFilter(request, response);
    }
}
```

### Tier 3: Production Hardening (30 min)

**Add comprehensive monitoring, testing, and HSM integration**

```java
// SECURE: Prometheus monitoring
package com.example.security;

import io.micrometer.core.instrument.Counter;
import io.micrometer.core.instrument.MeterRegistry;
import io.micrometer.core.instrument.Timer;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

@Component
public class CryptoMetrics {

    private final Counter encryptionCounter;
    private final Counter decryptionCounter;
    private final Counter encryptionFailures;
    private final Counter keyRotations;
    private final Timer encryptionDuration;

    public CryptoMetrics(MeterRegistry registry) {
        this.encryptionCounter = Counter.builder("token.encryption.total")
            .description("Total token encryption operations")
            .register(registry);

        this.decryptionCounter = Counter.builder("token.decryption.total")
            .description("Total token decryption operations")
            .register(registry);

        this.encryptionFailures = Counter.builder("token.crypto.failures")
            .description("Token encryption/decryption failures")
            .tag("severity", "critical")
            .register(registry);

        this.keyRotations = Counter.builder("token.key.rotations")
            .description("Encryption key rotation events")
            .register(registry);

        this.encryptionDuration = Timer.builder("token.crypto.duration")
            .description("Token encryption operation duration")
            .register(registry);
    }

    public void recordEncryption() {
        encryptionCounter.increment();
    }

    public void recordDecryption() {
        decryptionCounter.increment();
    }

    public void recordFailure() {
        encryptionFailures.increment();
    }

    public void recordKeyRotation() {
        keyRotations.increment();
    }

    public Timer.Sample startTimer() {
        return Timer.start();
    }

    public void recordDuration(Timer.Sample sample) {
        sample.stop(encryptionDuration);
    }
}

// Comprehensive integration tests
package com.example.security;

import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.boot.test.context.SpringBootTest;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

@SpringBootTest
public class TokenEncryptionSecurityTest {

    @Autowired
    private TokenEncryptionService encryptionService;

    @Test
    public void testVulnerableCodeIsExploitable() throws Exception {
        // ✅ Verify vulnerable implementation has hardcoded key
        String vulnerableClass = "com.example.security.CryptoService";
        byte[] classBytes = getClass().getClassLoader()
            .getResourceAsStream(vulnerableClass.replace('.', '/') + ".class")
            .readAllBytes();

        String bytecode = new String(classBytes);
        assertTrue(bytecode.contains("MySecretKey"),
            "Vulnerable code should contain hardcoded key");
    }

    @Test
    public void testTier1BlocksAttack() throws Exception {
        // ✅ Verify Tier 1 produces different ciphertext for same plaintext
        String token = "secret-api-token-12345";

        String ciphertext1 = encryptionService.encryptToken(token);
        String ciphertext2 = encryptionService.encryptToken(token);

        assertNotEquals(ciphertext1, ciphertext2,
            "Same plaintext must produce different ciphertext (random IVs)");

        // ✅ Verify both decrypt correctly
        assertEquals(token, encryptionService.decryptToken(ciphertext1));
        assertEquals(token, encryptionService.decryptToken(ciphertext2));
    }

    @Test
    public void testAuthenticatedEncryptionDetectsTampering() throws Exception {
        String token = "secret-api-token-12345";
        String ciphertext = encryptionService.encryptToken(token);

        // ✅ Tamper with ciphertext
        byte[] tamperedBytes = Base64.getDecoder().decode(ciphertext);
        tamperedBytes[20] ^= 0x01; // Flip one bit
        String tamperedCiphertext = Base64.getEncoder().encodeToString(tamperedBytes);

        // ✅ Verify tampering is detected
        assertThrows(Exception.class, () -> {
            encryptionService.decryptToken(tamperedCiphertext);
        }, "Tampered ciphertext must be rejected");
    }

    @Test
    public void testKeyNotHardcoded() throws Exception {
        // ✅ Verify no hardcoded keys in secure implementation
        String secureClass = "com.example.security.TokenEncryptionService";
        byte[] classBytes = getClass().getClassLoader()
            .getResourceAsStream(secureClass.replace('.', '/') + ".class")
            .readAllBytes();

        String bytecode = new String(classBytes);
        assertFalse(bytecode.contains("MySecretKey"),
            "Secure code must not contain hardcoded keys");
        assertFalse(bytecode.contains("SECRET_KEY"),
            "Secure code must not contain hardcoded keys");
    }

    @Test
    public void testWeakAlgorithmRejected() {
        // ✅ Verify DES/3DES cannot be instantiated
        assertThrows(Exception.class, () -> {
            Cipher.getInstance("DES");
        }, "DES algorithm should not be available");

        assertThrows(Exception.class, () -> {
            Cipher.getInstance("DESede");
        }, "3DES algorithm should not be available");
    }

    @Test
    public void testEncryptionPerformance() throws Exception {
        // ✅ Verify encryption completes within performance bounds
        String token = "secret-api-token-12345";
        long startTime = System.nanoTime();

        for (int i = 0; i < 1000; i++) {
            encryptionService.encryptToken(token);
        }

        long duration = System.nanoTime() - startTime;
        long avgMicros = duration / 1000 / 1000;

        assertTrue(avgMicros < 500,
            "Average encryption time should be <500μs, was: " + avgMicros + "μs");
    }
}
```

